A fully operational three-component monitoring pipeline (Prometheus, Alertmanager, Node Exporter) running as systemd services, with validated configuration files and confirmed metric ingestion from the local host.
A working alert lifecycle demonstration: PromQL rules evaluate against live metrics, alerts transition from pending to firing, Alertmanager routes them to the correct webhook receiver based on severity and alert type, and inhibition rules suppress redundant notifications as configured.
Conclusion
This lab required you to build a production-grade alerting pipeline entirely from first principles, making every architectural decision yourself. The multi-condition PromQL expressions and Alertmanager inhibition rules you designed reflect the core techniques used to reduce alert fatigue in real high-traffic systems. Extend this foundation by integrating a persistent notification channel such as PagerDuty or Slack, and by adding recording rules to pre-compute expensive PromQL expressions for faster evaluation at scale.
